==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*1 [[King Wahwah]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jrs]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 113.33~116.67 seconds<sup>3,400f~3,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*4 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Let the Cat Base tank the first Ragin' Gory for a while, then, once you've saved up 4,700¢, send out [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Bahamut will juggle Ragin' Gory to death before proceeding to knock back Wahwah, killing Bore Jr. in the process. When he does, send out [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]] in quick succession to continue the chain. The second Ragin' Gory will be the biggest problem from then on, and he'll appear right around the time you bring Wahwah to the enemy base. If you have him, [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] will do a fine enough job at holding him back while you brutally beat Wahwah; otherwise, you can meatshield with [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cats]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cats]] until the job is done.

Bring a few units to deal with the subsequent Angelic Beast Rajakong in case you aren't able to destroy the enemy base before it spawns, e.g. [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], and/or [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]].

